1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,240
 Let us start on our Docker journey by learning what is Docker.

2
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:11,680
 Docker is a containerization platform for building softwares,

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:18,880
 something like a virtual machine without the use of external hardware.

4
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:28,240
 Container virtualize the entire operating system of a machine to run multiple applications

5
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:32,020
 on a single host OS.

6
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:38,920
 Containers contain operating system like Linux, Windows or Mac OS.

7
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:43,960
 Inside this OS there are other programs installed.

8
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:51,000
 These programs can be .NET, Apache, engine X and so on.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,280
 In this figure we can see there is a Docker container and we have an operating system.

10
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:02,600
 Ubuntu Linux installed on it.

11
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:13,540
 .NET software is installed on the Ubuntu OS which as told earlier is running inside a Docker container.

12
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:19,560
 We also have engine X steps server installed on Ubuntu OS.

13
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:24,700
 So this means we have an OS with our needful programs.

